 "text": "..title\nA resolution to amend Ordinance No. BL2024-359 to authorize The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to modify the acceptance of public water and sanitary sewer mains, sanitary sewer manhole and easements, and to update Map and Parcel information, for property located at now Milson Lane (unnumbered), also known as Carothers Crossing Phase 10 Section 2A, Rev. 1, (MWS Project Nos. 24-WL-09 and 24-SL-21 and Proposal No. 2024M-052ES-002).\n..body\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2024-359, approved June 7, 2024, authorized the acceptance of approximately 1,237 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,155 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), four new fire hydrant assemblies, 10 new sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 7211 Carothers Road, also known as Carothers Crossing Phase 10 Section 2A; and,\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 66 additional linear feet of eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 125 additional linear feet of eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), one additional sanitary sewer manhole and easements, are now needed to construct Project Nos. 24-WL-09 and 24-SL-21; and,\nWHEREAS, the property located at 7211 Carothers Road, is now Milson Lane (unnumbered); and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2024M-052ES-002 on November 20, 2025, for revisions to the original mandatory referral; and,\nWHEREAS, Ordinance No. BL2024-359 provides that amendments to the legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThat Ordinance No. BL2024-359 is hereby amended by deleting Section 1 in its entirety and replacing it with the following:\nThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 1,303 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,280 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), four new fire hydrant assemblies, 11 new sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property now located at Milson Lane (unnumbered), also known as Carothers Crossing Phase 10 Section 2A, Rev. 1, as shown below and on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel:\t\t\t\t\tAddress:\n18800019900\t\t\t\t\tMilson Lane (unnumbered)\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this resolution. \nSection 3. This resolution shall take effect upon passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nOrdinance No. BL2024-359 was approved by the Metropolitan Council on June 7, 2024. The ordinance authorized the acceptance of approximately 1,237 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 1,155 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), four new fire hydrant assemblies, 10 new sanitary sewer manholes and easements for property located at 7211 Carothers Road, also known as Carothers Crossing Phase 10 Section 2A. BL2024-359 provides that amendments to the ordinance may be approved by resolution. \n\nThis proposed resolution would amend BL2024-359 to accept approximately 66 additional linear feet of eight-inch water main (DIP), 125 additional linear feet of eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), one additional sanitary sewer manhole and easements. The resolution would also update the map and parcel information to reflect that the project is now located at Milson Lane (unnumbered).\n\nThese changes have been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\n"
